    "description": "The operator egress ceiling's rate criterion (#481) at R = 1 MiB/s. One long-lived engine (engine_mode run) uploads to the lab's MinIO through s3_native with upload.max_egress_bytes_per_second set, and its own vtop_upload_egress_bytes_total is scraped once a second. Pass: every one-second bucket at or below R, and the 60 s total within 10% of R x 60 (the shaper's design predicts about 31/32 of R). The workload exists only to keep the shaper saturated: a concurrent seeder offers about 1.3 x R, so there is always an object waiting on the shaper. Judged by benchmarks/egress_cap_check.py on the run directory. Scenarios 20 and 21 are this file at 4 and 16 MiB/s, with the seeder sized to their own R; nothing else differs. Requires the containerized profile, docker compose -f benchmarks/docker-compose.benchmark.yml --profile containerized up -d.",
